  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "A force on an object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The position of that object at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> after starting from rest. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac></math> will be _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>F</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Displacement covered in vector form can be written as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>u</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Comparing it with,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>s</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>, we get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>&#38;</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>",
